[I] Razer mouse configuration tool

[T] razercfg is a configuration utility for Razer devices on Linux. It
[T] consists of the razerd daemon, the razercfg command-line tool and the
[T] optional PyQt based qrazercfg GUI for setting resolution, polling rate,
[T] LEDs and button mappings.

[U] https://bues.ch/cms/hacking/razercfg.html

[A] Razercfg Authors
[M] René Rebe <rene@exactco.de>

